      },
      "source": [
        "## **3. Data**\n",
        "\n",
        "The dataset used in this project is **Predict Students' Dropout and Academic Success** [3], published in the UCI Machine Learning Repository and described in detail by Realinho et al. [4]. It contains the records of 4,424 students from a Portuguese higher education institution, with 36 attributes and 1 class attribute (`Target`: Dropout, Enrolled, Graduate). The attributes combine information known at enrollment with the student's academic results at the end of the first and second semesters.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Link:** https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/697/predict+students+dropout+and+academic+success\n",
        "\n",
        "The attributes fall into five groups:\n",
        "- **Demographic:** e.g. `Gender`, `Age at enrollment`, `Marital status`, `International`\n",
        "- **Socioeconomic:** e.g. parents' qualifications and occupations, `Debtor`, `Tuition fees up to date`, `Scholarship holder`\n",
        "- **Academic path at enrollment:** e.g. `Course`, `Application mode`, `Previous qualification (grade)`, `Admission grade`\n",
        "- **Academic performance:** credited, enrolled, evaluated and approved curricular units, and the grade, for the 1st and 2nd semesters\n",
        "- **Macroeconomic:** `Unemployment rate`, `Inflation rate`, `GDP`\n",
        "\n",
        "Section 3.1 describes the dataset as presented in Phase 1, and Sections 3.2 to 3.4 present the data analysis from Phase 2."
      ]
    },
