        "The Gini tree shows how these attributes work together: students who passed four or fewer courses in the first semester are mostly classified as Dropout, and among them, 327 of the 344 students with unpaid tuition fees dropped out. This suggests that early academic progress is the strongest warning sign of dropout, and that financial difficulty makes the risk higher. These are associations found in the data, not proof of the causes of dropout.\n",
