        "Comparing the two criteria (Section 6.4), Gini reached 73.81%, 72.09% and 69.28% on the 90/10, 80/20 and 70/30 partitions, while Entropy reached 72.23%, 72.09% and 71.91%. Gini was better on 90/10, the two were equal on 80/20, and Entropy was better on 70/30. The averages (71.73% for Gini and 72.08% for Entropy) are almost the same, so the choice of criterion made little difference. All trees are far above the 49.93% baseline of always predicting Graduate, but Enrolled students remain hard to identify: Gini identified only 24% to 38% of them, and Entropy 48% on the 90/10 partition. Entropy found more Enrolled students but fewer Dropout students than Gini on that partition (55% against 75%), so the better criterion depends on which class matters most.\n",
